(6)What will be the output of the following code snippet?
a = ”10”
b=float(a)+5
result=str(b)+"123"
print(type(result))
(a)<c l a s s ’ f l o a t ’>  (b)<c l a s s ’ s t r ’>   (c)<c l a s s ’ i n t ’>    (d)The code will give an error.
ANS-a = "10": a is a string containing the characters '1' and '0'. b = float(a) + 5: float(a) converts "10" to the floating-point number 10.0. Then 10.0 + 5 results in 15.0, so b becomes 15.0 (a float).
result = str(b) + "123": str(b) converts the float 15.0 into the string "15.0". Then, "15.0" is concatenated (joined) with "123" to form the string "15.0123", so result becomes "15.0123" (a string).
This prints the data type of the result variable, which is a string. 

